Perfect. Now I have all the documentation and context needed. Let me produce the comprehensive HUD configuration guide.

---

## CLAUDE CODE TERMINAL HUD CONFIGURATION GUIDE

---

## 1. STATUS LINE — Configuration & Fields

The **status line** displays inline metrics at the end of each Claude response. It runs a script that receives session data on stdin (JSON) and outputs formatted text.

### Settings.json Key
```json
{
  "statusLine": {
    "type": "command",
    "command": "node /path/to/token-status.js"
  }
}
```

### Available Fields (from hook input JSON)

| Field | Source | Use |
|-------|--------|-----|
| `model.display_name` / `model.name` | Session data | Current model (e.g., "Claude 3.5 Sonnet") |
| `context_window.used_percentage` | Session data | Context fill %age (0–100) |
| `usage.input_tokens` | Session data | Prompt tokens this turn |
| `usage.output_tokens` | Session data | Completion tokens this turn |
| `usage.total_tokens` | Session data | Combined input + output |
| `cost` / `session_cost` | Session data | USD cost of this call |
| Git branch | Via `git branch --show-current` | Current git branch |
| Session ID | Via environment `$CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` | Session identifier |
| Timestamp | Via `new Date().toISOString()` | Turn completion time |

### Maximal Example Status Line Hook

```json
{
  "statusLine": {
    "type": "command",
    "command": "node $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/token-status.js"
  }
}
```

**Script Output Format** (`token-status.js`):
```javascript
#!/usr/bin/env node
const fs = require('fs');

const input = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim();
if (!input) {
  console.log('🔌 Offline');
  process.exit(0);
}

const data = JSON.parse(input);
const model = data?.model?.display_name || data?.model?.name || 'Claude';
const context = data?.context_window?.used_percentage || 0;
const inputTokens = data?.usage?.input_tokens || 0;
const outputTokens = data?.usage?.output_tokens || 0;
const totalTokens = data?.usage?.total_tokens || (inputTokens + outputTokens) || 0;
const cost = data?.cost || 0;

const parts = [];

// Model indicator
parts.push(`🧠 ${model}`);

// Context fill with color-coded status
const contextIcon = context < 50 ? '🟢' : (context < 85 ? '🟡' : '🔴');
parts.push(`${contextIcon} ${context}%`);

// Token accounting
if (totalTokens > 0) {
  parts.push(`🔄 ${totalTokens.toLocaleString()}`);
  parts.push(`↑${inputTokens} ↓${outputTokens}`);
}

// Cost if non-zero
if (cost > 0) {
  parts.push(`💰 $${cost.toFixed(4)}`);
}

console.log(parts.join(' │ '));
```

**Output Example:**
```
🧠 Claude 3.5 Sonnet │ 🟡 67% │ 🔄 2,847 │ ↑412 ↓2,435 │ 💰 $0.0087
```

---

## 2. CLAUDE CODE SETTINGS.JSON — Terminal Visual Settings

### Full Annotated Configuration

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json",

  // ===== MODEL & PERFORMANCE =====
  "model": "sonnet",                    // Default model slug
  "availableModels": [
    "opus",
    "sonnet",
    "haiku"
  ],
  "effortLevel": "high",                // "low", "medium", "high", "xhigh"
  "alwaysThinkingEnabled": false,       // Extended thinking on by default

  // ===== TERMINAL DISPLAY =====
  "tui": "default",                     // "fullscreen" for immersive mode, "default" for split
  "viewMode": "verbose",                // "default", "verbose", "focus"
  "autoScrollEnabled": true,            // Auto-follow output to bottom
  "spinnerTipsEnabled": true,           // Show hints during async operations
  "editorMode": "normal",               // "normal" or "vim"

  // ===== OUTPUT & FORMATTING =====
  "diffStyle": "unified",               // How diffs render ("unified" or "side-by-side")
  "syntaxHighlighting": true,           // Enable code block coloring
  "showLineNumbers": true,              // Line numbers in code blocks
  "codeBlockTheme": "monokai",          // Syntax theme

  // ===== TOKEN & COST TRACKING =====
  "showTokenCount": true,               // Display token metrics after each turn
  "showCostEstimate": true,             // Show USD estimate
  "trackSessionMetrics": true,          // Persist session stats

  // ===== GIT INTEGRATION =====
  "includeGitInstructions": true,       // Inject git workflows into context
  "attribution": {
    "commit": "Co-Authored-By: {{user}} <{{email}}>",
    "pr": "Fixes #{{issue}}"
  },

  // ===== PERMISSIONS & SAFETY =====
